Z||000000||Shiner||10-13-1999||11:19 PM||||Okay, I burnt a throttle cable up on my '84, I went to the junkyard, the only car there with a 4cyl and the cable in one piece was an 85 SC.  So I grabbed it.  The throttle cable looks different.  Is it, or can it be used?  If not, anybody wanna trade a NICE '85 4cyl cable for an '84?||||reg||8
Z||000001||Lynx||10-14-1999||03:47 AM||||Sorry to tell you, but they are different cables. So the bad news is you have a useless throttle cable, the good news is that you can get them from the fiero store for only $26 for a '84. I hope you didnt pay much for the one at the junkyard.||||reg||9
Z||000002||TOM||10-14-1999||10:11 AM||||Why are they different the cars are basically the same?||||reg||1
Z||000003||DJRice||10-15-1999||08:57 AM||||If car you got the cable from was a 4 cyl, I would say give it a try.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||10-15-1999||04:14 PM||||if the ends of the cable (the core wire) are the same, but the sleve ends are diferant, the worst thing you might need is a diferant bracket on one end or the other.<P>All 4 cyl thu 86 use the same TBI unit. Worst case is you need brackets, and the throttle pedal, and maybe the throttle shaft pully of the newer TBI. More effort maybe, but not a bad thing in the end.<P>If you said you got it off an 87 or 88 Then I'd say you can use it at all.... the 87+ 4 cyl use a whole diferant TBI and cables.||||reg||1
